hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27796","Haddathana Hajjaj who said: Haddathana Layth who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib that Suwayd ibn Qays informed him from Muawiya ibn Hudayj that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day and saluted and left while a raka of the prayer remained; so a man met him and said: You have forgotten a raka of the prayer; so he returned and entered the mosque and ordered Bilal, and he called the iqama, and he prayed a raka with the people; so I informed the people of that, and they said to me: Do you know the man; I said: No, except that I see him; so he passed by me and I said: He is this; so they said: Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"27797","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq who said: Haddathana Ibn Lahia from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Suwayd ibn Qays from Muawiya ibn Hudayj who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A morning going in the path of Allah or an evening going is better than the world and what is in it."
"27798","Haddathana Abd Allah ibn Yazid who said: Haddathana Said ibn Abi Ayyub who said: Haddathani Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Suwayd ibn Qays al-Tujibi of Kinda from Muawiya ibn Hudayj who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is healing in anything, then in an incision of a cupper, or a drink of honey, or a cauterization with fire striking pain; and I do not like to be cauterized."
"27799","[Truncated in source] Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad who said: Haddathana Abd Allah who said: Haddathana Ibn Lahia who said: Haddathani al-Harith ibn Yazid from Ali ibn Rabah who said: I heard Muawiya ibn Hudayj say: We emigrated in the time of Abu Bakr; while we were with him, he ascended the minbar [text ends here in source]."
"27800","Haddathana Affan who said: Haddathana Hammad ibn Salama who said: Haddathana Thabit from Salih Abu Hujayr from Muawiya ibn Hudayj, and he had companionship, who said: Whoever washes a dead one and shrouds him and follows him and takes charge of his body returns forgiven for him; Abu Abd al-Rahman said: My father said: It is not marfu."
